@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home";
}

<div class="page-head">
    <h1>Clean Architecture Demo</h1>
</div>

<p class="text-muted prose mb-4">
    An ASP.NET Core MVC reference application built on a strict Domain → Application → Infrastructure → Web
    dependency direction. Pick a directory to work in.
</p>

<div class="row g-3 mb-4">
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <a asp-controller="Products" asp-action="Index" class="panel panel-link panel-pad d-block h-100 text-decoration-none">
            <h2 class="mb-1">Products</h2>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0" style="font-size: .875rem">
                Catalogue with stock levels, categories and customer ownership. Filtered, sorted and paged on the server.
            </p>
        </a>
    </div>
    <div class="col-md-6">
        <a asp-controller="Customers" asp-action="Index" class="panel panel-link panel-pad d-block h-100 text-decoration-none">
            <h2 class="mb-1">Customers</h2>
            <p class="text-muted mb-0" style="font-size: .875rem">
                Directory edited in place through a modal, without leaving the list.
            </p>
        </a>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="panel">
    <div class="panel-head">
        <h2>How it is put together</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-pad">
        <dl class="row detail-list">
            <dt class="col-sm-3">Layers</dt>
            <dd class="col-sm-9 mb-3">Domain, Application, Infrastructure and Web, each registering itself through one extension method.</dd>

            <dt class="col-sm-3">Data access</dt>
            <dd class="col-sm-9 mb-3">A single unit of work exposing the repositories; the service owns the save.</dd>

            <dt class="col-sm-3">Pagination</dt>
            <dd class="col-sm-9 mb-3">Pages are materialised in Infrastructure, so no <code>IQueryable</code> ever reaches the Application layer.</dd>

            <dt class="col-sm-3">Mapping</dt>
            <dd class="col-sm-9 mb-3">Mapster, with registrations scanned from the Application assembly.</dd>

            <dt class="col-sm-3">Errors</dt>
            <dd class="col-sm-9 mb-0">Domain exceptions mapped to status codes by one middleware, answering with JSON or a redirect depending on the request.</dd>
        </dl>
    </div>
</div>
